{"action":"issue","adjudicationId":"no-three-in-line/rotational-cardinality-obstructions","baseRevisionId":null,"evidence":[{"digest":null,"id":"c98dd877ad81611a9a469b1bd790cd909b56b1ce","kind":"transaction","relation":"context"},{"digest":"sha256:d24a70c16a08ff85401e969cfe12d8f8253056bb8d75e469ec226eba7a3b44c5","id":"sha256:d24a70c16a08ff85401e969cfe12d8f8253056bb8d75e469ec226eba7a3b44c5","kind":"judgment","relation":"supports"}],"issuedAtLedgerHead":"c98dd877ad81611a9a469b1bd790cd909b56b1ce","nodeId":"no-three-in-line/rotational-cardinality-obstructions","nodeType":"lemma","parentId":"root","reportRef":{"artifact":"report.md","digest":"sha256:3159760c2a8bb17234632dba5ffdb7c9471f65d7eddb341154cca0d186c91b82","section":"## Node: no-three-in-line/rotational-cardinality-obstructions"},"revisionId":"sha256:0c6485529418bc632ed59ad26b472349b6cc032121a0f08032a2d34417ac055a","revisionNumber":1,"status":"active","subjects":[{"id":"c98dd877ad81611a9a469b1bd790cd909b56b1ce","kind":"transaction","ledgerPosition":3}],"summary":"An odd-cardinality no-three-in-line set invariant under a half-turn has at most one point, so a 153-point set cannot have half-turn symmetry. A quarter-turn-invariant no-three-in-line set has cardinality divisible by four or equal to one, excluding quarter-turn symmetry at cardinalities 153 and 154.","title":"Half-turn and quarter-turn cardinality obstructions"}
{"action":"issue","adjudicationId":"no-three-in-line/d77-154-centered-half-turn-condition","baseRevisionId":null,"evidence":[{"digest":null,"id":"c98dd877ad81611a9a469b1bd790cd909b56b1ce","kind":"transaction","relation":"context"},{"digest":"sha256:d24a70c16a08ff85401e969cfe12d8f8253056bb8d75e469ec226eba7a3b44c5","id":"sha256:d24a70c16a08ff85401e969cfe12d8f8253056bb8d75e469ec226eba7a3b44c5","kind":"judgment","relation":"supports"}],"issuedAtLedgerHead":"c98dd877ad81611a9a469b1bd790cd909b56b1ce","nodeId":"no-three-in-line/d77-154-centered-half-turn-condition","nodeType":"lemma","parentId":"root","reportRef":{"artifact":"report.md","digest":"sha256:3159760c2a8bb17234632dba5ffdb7c9471f65d7eddb341154cca0d186c91b82","section":"## Node: no-three-in-line/d77-154-centered-half-turn-condition"},"revisionId":"sha256:6144825a3263d937c7dbde8488ba6a01040b99434199bc145f8d64eaf9738698","revisionNumber":1,"status":"active","subjects":[{"id":"c98dd877ad81611a9a469b1bd790cd909b56b1ce","kind":"transaction","ledgerPosition":3}],"summary":"If a 154-point no-three-in-line subset of G_77 is half-turn invariant, every row and column contains exactly two selected points, the half-turn is centered at (38,38), and that center is unoccupied. The condition does not assert existence or require every hypothetical 154-point set to have half-turn symmetry.","title":"Centered half-turn condition for a 154-point subset of G_77"}
{"action":"issue","adjudicationId":"no-three-in-line/d77-rotational-symmetry-at-153-154","baseRevisionId":null,"evidence":[{"digest":null,"id":"c98dd877ad81611a9a469b1bd790cd909b56b1ce","kind":"transaction","relation":"context"},{"digest":"sha256:d24a70c16a08ff85401e969cfe12d8f8253056bb8d75e469ec226eba7a3b44c5","id":"sha256:d24a70c16a08ff85401e969cfe12d8f8253056bb8d75e469ec226eba7a3b44c5","kind":"judgment","relation":"qualifies"}],"issuedAtLedgerHead":"c98dd877ad81611a9a469b1bd790cd909b56b1ce","nodeId":"no-three-in-line/d77-rotational-symmetry-at-153-154","nodeType":"claim","parentId":"root","reportRef":{"artifact":"report.md","digest":"sha256:3159760c2a8bb17234632dba5ffdb7c9471f65d7eddb341154cca0d186c91b82","section":"## Node: no-three-in-line/d77-rotational-symmetry-at-153-154"},"revisionId":"sha256:6f9d6f30fb5ed361a7cea40e2b6cbdce97865e699b52995a19537089ff411ae3","revisionNumber":1,"status":"active","subjects":[{"id":"c98dd877ad81611a9a469b1bd790cd909b56b1ce","kind":"transaction","ledgerPosition":3}],"summary":"The accepted order-two and order-four results exclude half-turn symmetry at 153, quarter-turn symmetry at 153 and 154, and noncentered half-turn symmetry at 154. Exhaustiveness is established only when rotational symmetry is restricted to square-grid dihedral rotations; arbitrary-center finite-order lattice rotations were not explicitly classified. The rct4 class is strictly narrower than centered half-turn symmetry.","title":"Qualified rotational-symmetry classification at cardinalities 153 and 154"}
{"action":"issue","adjudicationId":"no-three-in-line/d77-rct4-154-model","baseRevisionId":null,"evidence":[{"digest":null,"id":"c98dd877ad81611a9a469b1bd790cd909b56b1ce","kind":"transaction","relation":"context"},{"digest":"sha256:d24a70c16a08ff85401e969cfe12d8f8253056bb8d75e469ec226eba7a3b44c5","id":"sha256:d24a70c16a08ff85401e969cfe12d8f8253056bb8d75e469ec226eba7a3b44c5","kind":"judgment","relation":"formalizes"}],"issuedAtLedgerHead":"c98dd877ad81611a9a469b1bd790cd909b56b1ce","nodeId":"no-three-in-line/d77-rct4-154-model","nodeType":"method","parentId":"root","reportRef":{"artifact":"report.md","digest":"sha256:3159760c2a8bb17234632dba5ffdb7c9471f65d7eddb341154cca0d186c91b82","section":"## Node: no-three-in-line/d77-rct4-154-model"},"revisionId":"sha256:1a675fb492dd2edffde577cfbeefd241b1b907b0e920b318786669b0e8884d65","revisionNumber":1,"status":"active","subjects":[{"id":"c98dd877ad81611a9a469b1bd790cd909b56b1ce","kind":"transaction","ledgerPosition":3}],"summary":"The accepted model exactly encodes the stated 154-point rct4 subclass using 1,444 off-diagonal quarter-turn-orbit variables, 38 main-diagonal half-turn-pair variables, exact cardinality constraints, and 388,148 deduplicated weighted line constraints. Its satisfiability remains unresolved; timeouts and UNKNOWN results establish neither satisfiability nor unsatisfiability, and infeasibility would exclude only the strict rct4 subclass.","title":"Exact rct4 model for 154-point configurations in G_77"}
